WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.093
Say what the output looks like, and say it positively.

2
00:00:03.373 --> 00:00:12.547
If code will read the output, specify the format exactly: the fields, the allowed values, the length limits, and what to return when the input doesn’t fit.

3
00:00:12.827 --> 00:00:25.435
“Return JSON” is a wish; “Return only a JSON object with keys category (one of billing, bug, account, other) and summary (one sentence, under 25 words)” is a contract you can check.

4
00:00:25.715 --> 00:00:29.491
Week 3 moves this into schemas that the API enforces.

5
00:00:29.771 --> 00:00:33.739
Anthropic’s docs list three formatting techniques that transfer well.

6
00:00:34.019 --> 00:00:41.933
First, tell the model what to do rather than what not to do: “write in flowing prose paragraphs” works better than “don’t use Markdown.

7
00:00:42.213 --> 00:00:46.800
” Second, name the output container: “put the summary inside summary tags.

8
00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:54.141
” Third, match your prompt’s style to the output you want, because a prompt full of bullet points tends to get bullet points back.

9
00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:57.749
The positive-instruction rule applies beyond formatting.

10
00:00:58.029 --> 00:01:05.560
A prohibition tells the model what to avoid but leaves the right behavior unstated, and a list of prohibitions grows forever.

11
00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:11.237
Write the behavior you want, and keep prohibitions for real hard limits, each with its reason.

12
00:01:11.517 --> 00:01:22.483
One technique you may have used is gone on current Claude models: prefill, where you write the first characters of the assistant’s reply (an opening brace, say) to force a format.

13
00:01:22.763 --> 00:01:23.957
Since the Claude 4.

14
00:01:24.237 --> 00:01:30.147
6 generation, a request whose last message is a prefilled assistant turn returns an error.

15
00:01:30.427 --> 00:01:37.232
The documented replacements are clear format instructions, output inside named tags, or structured outputs.

16
00:01:37.512 --> 00:01:46.899
Some open-weight stacks still support continuing a partial assistant message, which is one of many small differences that make prompts less portable than they look.
